diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a55755..09b0e31 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,15 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": <string or null>}`: one page
+  of items, ordered by `id` ascending.
+  - `limit` (optional): integer 1..100, default 20.
+  - `cursor` (optional): the `next_cursor` value from a previous response; treat
+    it as opaque. Omit it for the first page.
+  - `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page. To read everything, request
+    `/items`, then repeat with `cursor` set to each `next_cursor` until it is `null`.
+  - A `limit` outside 1..100 or not an integer, or a malformed `cursor`, returns
+    400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
